IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `roc-core`

-- Rules of Court 2021 (Singapore), G.N. No. S 914/2021, current version as at 5 November 2026.
-- ORDER 63: SECURITIES AND FUTURES ACT -- ORDER FOR DISGORGEMENT AGAINST THIRD PARTY (8 rules): the Authority or a
-- claimant applies under section 236L of the Securities and Futures Act for an order that a third party who
-- received a benefit of a contravention of Part XII give it up, and the claimants then claim compensation from the sum.
-- Source: a plain-text rendering made by a converter script from Singapore Statutes Online.
-- It is not the official text, and nothing here has been checked against the official text.
--
-- HOW TO READ A RESULT.  A MAYBE BOOLEAN answer is:
--   JUST TRUE   the text says yes on these facts.
--   JUST FALSE  the text says no in its own words (the FALSE-kind comment quotes them).
--   NOTHING     the text does not answer on these facts (the NOTHING-kind comment says why).
-- A caller must never turn NOTHING into FALSE.
-- O 3 r 2(1) is a caveat on every answer: every requirement in the Rules is subject to the Court's
-- discretion to order otherwise in the interests of justice; it is not threaded as an input.
-- What follows non-compliance with a Rule is O 3 r 2(4), except where this Order says so itself (rules 2(5), 3(6)).
--
-- BORROWED FACTS.  The Securities and Futures Act is not among the sources.  Its sections (236L(1), (2), (6),
-- (11), (12)) are named in the inputs and asked as facts.  Order 62 rules 6, 7, 8, 10 and 12 (rule 8 of this Order)
-- are in roc11's own Order 62 module, but this Order does not import it: a part cannot import another part.
-- Other Orders this Order applies (Order 6 rules 11 to 14, Order 9, Order 15 rule 7) are in other parts.
--
-- TIME.  O 3 r 3(1) says the Interpretation Act does not apply to the calculation of time in these Rules.
-- Whether an act was in time is a comparison with an input `o 3 r 3 the last day for doing the act`
-- (seam S-T1: roc1's O 3 r 3 computes it, and the merged file wires it).

-- ===========================================================================
§ `Order 63 -- Securities and Futures Act, order for disgorgement against third party`
-- ===========================================================================

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Rule 1 -- definitions and application of this Order`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:7306 | 1. —(1) In this Order — “Act” means the Securities and Futures Act, and any reference to a section is a reference to a section in the Act;
@ref O 63 r 1(1) "Act" (src:7306)
`o 63 r 1(1) the Act` MEANS "the Securities and Futures Act"

-- "any reference to a section is a reference to a section in the Act".  The text carves out no reference that
-- names another Act expressly; it is silent on one.
-- src:7306 | 1. —(1) In this Order — “Act” means the Securities and Futures Act, and any reference to a section is a reference to a section in the Act;
@ref O 63 r 1(1) (src:7306)
GIVEN `the reference is to a section` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the reference names another Act expressly` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 63 r 1(1) a reference to a section is a reference to a section in the Act` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the reference names another Act expressly`
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the Rule does not say what a reference does that names another Act
        IF `the reference is to a section`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any reference to a section" speaks only of a reference to a section

-- src:7307 | “Authority” means the Monetary Authority of Singapore established by section 3 of the Monetary Authority of Singapore Act;
@ref O 63 r 1(1) "Authority" (src:7307)
`o 63 r 1(1) the Authority` MEANS "the Monetary Authority of Singapore established by section 3 of the Monetary Authority of Singapore Act"

-- src:7308 | “claimant” has the meaning given by section 236L(12);
@ref O 63 r 1(1) "claimant" (src:7308)
`o 63 r 1(1) "claimant" the section that gives its meaning` MEANS "section 236L(12)"

-- src:7310 | “third party” has the meaning given by section 236L(1).
@ref O 63 r 1(1) "third party" (src:7310)
`o 63 r 1(1) "third party" the section that gives its meaning` MEANS "section 236L(1)"

-- "order for disgorgement" means an order applied for under section 236L(1).  A "means" definition, so a case
-- outside it is JUST FALSE.
-- src:7309 | “order for disgorgement” means an order applied for under section 236L(1);
@ref O 63 r 1(1) "order for disgorgement" (src:7309)
GIVEN `the order is one applied for under section 236L(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 63 r 1(1) "order for disgorgement" the order is an order for disgorgement` MEANS
    IF `the order is one applied for under section 236L(1)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "means an order applied for under section 236L(1)"

-- src:7311 | (2) These Rules apply to proceedings under section 236L, subject to the following Rules of this Order.
@ref O 63 r 1(2) (src:7311)
GIVEN `the proceeding is under section 236L` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 63 r 1(2) these Rules apply to the proceeding` MEANS
    IF `the proceeding is under section 236L`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "These Rules apply to proceedings under section 236L" names the proceedings it reaches and says nothing of others

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Rule 2 -- commencement of action under section 236L`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- (1): "may be made by originating application, naming as the defendant ... the third party".  A permission about
-- the mode, not a bar: any other mode or defendant is left to the Rules elsewhere, so NOTHING.
-- src:7313 | 2. —(1) An application for an order for disgorgement under section 236L may be made by originating application, naming as the defendant in the originating application the third party. (2) Unless modified expressly in this Rule, Order 6, Rules 11 to 14, Order 9 and Order 15, Rule 7 apply to the originating application.
@ref O 63 r 2(1) (src:7313)
GIVEN `the application is for an order for disgorgement under section 236L` IS A BOOLEAN
      document IS A `Document kind`
      `the defendant named is the third party` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 63 r 2(1) the application for an order for disgorgement may be made in this way` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the application is for an order for disgorgement under section 236L`)
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): rule 2(1) speaks of "An application for an order for disgorgement under section 236L"
        IF document EQUALS `Originating application` AND `the defendant named is the third party`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "may be made by originating application, naming as the defendant ... the third party" gives a permission and says nothing of any other mode or defendant

-- (2): other Orders apply unless this Rule expressly modifies them (S-L1: what they say is in other parts).
-- src:7313 | 2. —(1) An application for an order for disgorgement under section 236L may be made by originating application, naming as the defendant in the originating application the third party. (2) Unless modified expressly in this Rule, Order 6, Rules 11 to 14, Order 9 and Order 15, Rule 7 apply to the originating application.
@ref O 63 r 2(2) (src:7313)
GIVEN `the application is the originating application of rule 2(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      provision IS A STRING
      `rule 2 expressly modifies the provision` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 63 r 2(2) the provision applies to the originating application` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the application is the originating application of rule 2(1)`)
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): rule 2(2) speaks of "the originating application" of paragraph (1)
        IF NOT (elem provision (LIST
            "Order 6 rule 11",
            "Order 6 rule 12",
            "Order 6 rule 13",
            "Order 6 rule 14",
            "Order 9",
            "Order 15 rule 7"))
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): only "Order 6, Rules 11 to 14, Order 9 and Order 15, Rule 7" are named
        IF `rule 2 expressly modifies the provision`
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Unless modified expressly in this Rule"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- (3): the supporting affidavit.  Part (b) is required only "where the application is made by a claimant".
DECLARE `o 63 r 2(3) affidavit` HAS
    `o 63 r 2(3)(a) sets out the grounds on which the application is made` IS A BOOLEAN
    `o 63 r 2(3)(a)(i) sets out particulars of the contravention of the relevant provision of Part XII of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
    `o 63 r 2(3)(a)(ii) sets out the circumstances leading to the trades carried out for the third party in question` IS A BOOLEAN
    `o 63 r 2(3)(a)(iii) sets out the circumstances leading to the third party receiving the whole or any part of the benefit of the contravention` IS A BOOLEAN
    `o 63 r 2(3)(a)(iv) sets out particulars of the benefit received by the third party` IS A BOOLEAN
    `o 63 r 2(3)(b) the application is made by a claimant` IS A BOOLEAN
    `o 63 r 2(3)(b)(i) sets out particulars of the securities transaction, futures contract, or contract or arrangement in connection with leveraged foreign exchange trading, in respect of which the claimant suffered a loss` IS A BOOLEAN
    `o 63 r 2(3)(b)(ii) sets out the circumstances leading to the entering into of the transaction in question` IS A BOOLEAN
    `o 63 r 2(3)(b)(iii) sets out the circumstances leading to the loss suffered` IS A BOOLEAN
    `o 63 r 2(3)(b)(iv) sets out particulars of the loss suffered` IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:7314 | (3) The application under paragraph (1) must be supported by an affidavit setting out — ( a )
-- src:7315 | the grounds on which the application is made, including — (i)
-- src:7316 | particulars of the contravention of the relevant provision of Part XII of the Act;
-- src:7317 | (ii)
-- src:7318 | circumstances leading to the trades carried out for the third party in question;
-- src:7319 | (iii)
-- src:7320 | circumstances leading to the third party receiving the whole or any part of the benefit of the contravention; and
-- src:7321 | (iv)
-- src:7322 | particulars of the benefit received by the third party; and
-- src:7323 | ( b )
-- src:7324 | where the application is made by a claimant — (i)
-- src:7325 | particulars of the securities transaction, futures contract, or contract or arrangement in connection with leveraged foreign exchange trading, in respect of which the claimant suffered a loss;
-- src:7326 | (ii)
-- src:7327 | circumstances leading to the entering into of the transaction in question;
-- src:7328 | (iii)
-- src:7329 | circumstances leading to the loss suffered; and
-- src:7330 | (iv)
-- src:7331 | particulars of the loss suffered.
@ref O 63 r 2(3) (src:7314-7331)
GIVEN affidavit IS A `o 63 r 2(3) affidavit`
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`o 63 r 2(3) the matters the affidavit has not yet set out` MEANS
    concat (LIST
        (IF affidavit's `o 63 r 2(3)(a) sets out the grounds on which the application is made` THEN EMPTY ELSE LIST "(a) the grounds on which the application is made"),
        (IF affidavit's `o 63 r 2(3)(a)(i) sets out particulars of the contravention of the relevant provision of Part XII of the Act` THEN EMPTY ELSE LIST "(a)(i) particulars of the contravention of the relevant provision of Part XII of the Act"),
        (IF affidavit's `o 63 r 2(3)(a)(ii) sets out the circumstances leading to the trades carried out for the third party in question` THEN EMPTY ELSE LIST "(a)(ii) circumstances leading to the trades carried out for the third party in question"),
        (IF affidavit's `o 63 r 2(3)(a)(iii) sets out the circumstances leading to the third party receiving the whole or any part of the benefit of the contravention` THEN EMPTY ELSE LIST "(a)(iii) circumstances leading to the third party receiving the whole or any part of the benefit of the contravention"),
        (IF affidavit's `o 63 r 2(3)(a)(iv) sets out particulars of the benefit received by the third party` THEN EMPTY ELSE LIST "(a)(iv) particulars of the benefit received by the third party"),
        (IF (NOT (affidavit's `o 63 r 2(3)(b) the application is made by a claimant`)) OR affidavit's `o 63 r 2(3)(b)(i) sets out particulars of the securities transaction, futures contract, or contract or arrangement in connection with leveraged foreign exchange trading, in respect of which the claimant suffered a loss` THEN EMPTY ELSE LIST "(b)(i) particulars of the securities transaction, futures contract, or contract or arrangement in connection with leveraged foreign exchange trading, in respect of which the claimant suffered a loss"),
        (IF (NOT (affidavit's `o 63 r 2(3)(b) the application is made by a claimant`)) OR affidavit's `o 63 r 2(3)(b)(ii) sets out the circumstances leading to the entering into of the transaction in question` THEN EMPTY ELSE LIST "(b)(ii) circumstances leading to the entering into of the transaction in question"),
        (IF (NOT (affidavit's `o 63 r 2(3)(b) the application is made by a claimant`)) OR affidavit's `o 63 r 2(3)(b)(iii) sets out the circumstances leading to the loss suffered` THEN EMPTY ELSE LIST "(b)(iii) circumstances leading to the loss suffered"),
        (IF (NOT (affidavit's `o 63 r 2(3)(b) the application is made by a claimant`)) OR affidavit's `o 63 r 2(3)(b)(iv) sets out particulars of the loss suffered` THEN EMPTY ELSE LIST "(b)(iv) particulars of the loss suffered"))

-- src:7314 | (3) The application under paragraph (1) must be supported by an affidavit setting out — ( a )
-- src:7315 | the grounds on which the application is made, including — (i)
-- src:7316 | particulars of the contravention of the relevant provision of Part XII of the Act;
