-- src:7331 | particulars of the loss suffered.
@ref O 63 r 2(3) (src:7314-7331)
GIVEN affidavit IS A `o 63 r 2(3) affidavit`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 63 r 2(3) the affidavit supporting the application sets out what the Rule requires` MEANS
    IF count (`o 63 r 2(3) the matters the affidavit has not yet set out` affidavit) EQUALS 0
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): a bare "must be supported by an affidavit setting out"; QB: NOTHING (O 3 r 2(4) says what the Court may do about non-compliance) / other: JUST FALSE

-- (4): "Unless the Court otherwise orders, ... must be served personally on (a) the third party; and (b) any other person
-- appearing to be interested as the Court may direct, at least 28 clear days or such longer time as the Court may direct,
-- before the hearing of the application."
-- src:7332 | (4) Unless the Court otherwise orders, the application under paragraph (1) and supporting affidavit under paragraph (3) must be served personally on — ( a )
-- src:7333 | the third party; and
-- src:7334 | ( b )
-- src:7335 | any other person appearing to be interested as the Court may direct,
-- src:7336 | at least 28 clear days or such longer time as the Court may direct, before the hearing of the application.
@ref O 63 r 2(4) (src:7332-7336)
`o 63 r 2(4) the period for serving the application before the hearing` MEANS Period WITH
    `period length` IS 28
    `period unit` IS `Clear days`
    `period direction` IS `Before the anchor`

-- src:7332 | (4) Unless the Court otherwise orders, the application under paragraph (1) and supporting affidavit under paragraph (3) must be served personally on — ( a )
@ref O 63 r 2(4) (src:7332)
GIVEN `the Court otherwise orders` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 63 r 2(4) the duty to serve the application personally in time arises` MEANS
    IF `the Court otherwise orders`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Unless the Court otherwise orders"
    ELSE JUST TRUE

-- src:7332 | (4) Unless the Court otherwise orders, the application under paragraph (1) and supporting affidavit under paragraph (3) must be served personally on — ( a )
-- src:7333 | the third party; and
-- src:7334 | ( b )
-- src:7335 | any other person appearing to be interested as the Court may direct,
-- src:7336 | at least 28 clear days or such longer time as the Court may direct, before the hearing of the application.
@ref O 63 r 2(4) (src:7332-7336)
GIVEN `the Court otherwise orders` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the application and affidavit are served personally on the third party` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Court has directed service on another person appearing to be interested` IS A BOOLEAN
      `they are served personally on that other person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date they were served` IS A DATE
      `o 3 r 3 the last day for doing the act` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 63 r 2(4) the application and affidavit are served as the Rule requires` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the Court otherwise orders`
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the duty does not arise; QD: NOTHING, and the companion `o 63 r 2(4) the duty to serve the application personally in time arises` answers JUST FALSE / other: JUST TRUE (nothing is unmet)
        IF `the date they were served` GREATER THAN `o 3 r 3 the last day for doing the act`
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "at least 28 clear days or such longer time as the Court may direct, before the hearing of the application"
        IF `the application and affidavit are served personally on the third party` AND ((NOT (`the Court has directed service on another person appearing to be interested`)) OR `they are served personally on that other person`)
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): not yet served personally on the third party (or on the other person the Court directed); a bare "must be served personally"; QB: NOTHING (O 3 r 2(4) and rule 2(5)) / other: JUST FALSE

GIVEN `the Court otherwise orders` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the application and affidavit are served personally on the third party` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Court has directed service on another person appearing to be interested` IS A BOOLEAN
      `they are served personally on that other person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date they were served` IS A DATE
      `o 3 r 3 the last day for doing the act` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`o 63 r 2(4) the applicant complied with paragraph (4)` MEANS
    `the Court otherwise orders` OR (`o 63 r 2(4) the application and affidavit are served as the Rule requires` `the Court otherwise orders` `the application and affidavit are served personally on the third party` `the Court has directed service on another person appearing to be interested` `they are served personally on that other person` `the date they were served` `o 3 r 3 the last day for doing the act` EQUALS JUST TRUE)

-- (5): "If the applicant ... or the applicant's solicitor does not comply with paragraph (4), the application is deemed
