-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Rule 3 -- application for directions on claims under section 236L`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- (1): "If an order for disgorgement has been made final in accordance with section 236L(11), the applicant for the order
-- or any claimant may apply ...".  A failed "If" counts as the text's no (a marginal reading); a person who is neither is outside the grant.
-- src:7341 | 3. —(1) If an order for disgorgement has been made final in accordance with section 236L(11), the applicant for the order or any claimant may apply to the Court for directions on claims for compensation to be paid out of the sum under the order, and the Court may, subject to section 236L(6), fix a return date for hearing the application. (2) Every application under paragraph (1) must be made by summons.
@ref O 63 r 3(1) (src:7341)
GIVEN `the order for disgorgement has been made final in accordance with section 236L(11)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is the applicant for the order or a claimant` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 63 r 3(1) the person may apply for directions on claims for compensation` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the order for disgorgement has been made final in accordance with section 236L(11)`)
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If an order for disgorgement has been made final in accordance with section 236L(11)"
        IF `the person is the applicant for the order or a claimant`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the permission is given to "the applicant for the order or any claimant" and says nothing of anyone else

