        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "at least 21 clear days or such longer time as the Court may direct before the return date"
        IF `the advertisement is in Form 93` AND (`it appeared at least once in one English and one Chinese local daily newspaper` OR `the Court directed another newspaper and it appeared there`)
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): a bare "must be advertised in Form 93 ... at least once in one English and one Chinese local daily newspaper"; QB: NOTHING (O 3 r 2(4) and rule 3(6)) / other: JUST FALSE

