-- (5): what the advertisement states.  The solicitor's name and address are required where the applicant has a solicitor.
DECLARE `o 63 r 3(5) advertisement` HAS
    `o 63 r 3(5) states the day on which the application was filed` IS A BOOLEAN
    `o 63 r 3(5) states the name and address of the applicant for directions` IS A BOOLEAN
    `o 63 r 3(5) the applicant has a solicitor` IS A BOOLEAN
    `o 63 r 3(5) states the name and address of the applicant's solicitor` IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:7348 | (5) The advertisement must state the day on which the application was filed and the name and address of the applicant for directions and of the applicant’s solicitor.
@ref O 63 r 3(5) (src:7348)
GIVEN advertisement IS A `o 63 r 3(5) advertisement`
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`o 63 r 3(5) the matters the advertisement has not yet stated` MEANS
    concat (LIST
        (IF advertisement's `o 63 r 3(5) states the day on which the application was filed` THEN EMPTY ELSE LIST "the day on which the application was filed"),
        (IF advertisement's `o 63 r 3(5) states the name and address of the applicant for directions` THEN EMPTY ELSE LIST "the name and address of the applicant for directions"),
        (IF (NOT (advertisement's `o 63 r 3(5) the applicant has a solicitor`)) OR advertisement's `o 63 r 3(5) states the name and address of the applicant's solicitor` THEN EMPTY ELSE LIST "the name and address of the applicant's solicitor"))

