    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`o 63 r 5(1) the Court may give directions or make orders after the hearing` hearing `all the persons on whom the application has been served and all claimants who have filed their affidavits of claim appear` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the Court may, after hearing"
        IF kind EQUALS `o 63 r 5(1) another kind of direction or order`
        THEN (IF `the Court thinks it best adapted to secure the just, expeditious and economical disposal of the proceedings` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING) -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "including" does not close the list, and an unlisted kind is within the power only if the Court thinks it best adapted
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:7388 | (2) Where the third party (or, where applicable, any other interested party referred to in Rule 3(3)( b )) — ( a )
-- src:7389 | having been duly served with a notice to show cause under Rule 2(6), does not appear at the hearing for the notice; or
-- src:7390 | ( b )
-- src:7391 | having been duly served with the application under Rule 3(1), does not appear on the hearing of the application,
-- src:7392 | or, having appeared, fails or refuses to comply with an order made in the proceedings, the Court may make such order as the Court deems appropriate.
@ref O 63 r 5(2) (src:7388-7392)
GIVEN `the person is the third party or another interested party referred to in Rule 3(3)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `duly served with a notice to show cause under Rule 2(6)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `does not appear at the hearing for the notice` IS A BOOLEAN
      `duly served with the application under Rule 3(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `does not appear on the hearing of the application` IS A BOOLEAN
      `having appeared fails or refuses to comply with an order made in the proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 63 r 5(2) the Court may make such order as it deems appropriate` MEANS
    IF    `the person is the third party or another interested party referred to in Rule 3(3)(b)`
      AND (   (`duly served with a notice to show cause under Rule 2(6)` AND `does not appear at the hearing for the notice`)
           OR (`duly served with the application under Rule 3(1)` AND `does not appear on the hearing of the application`)
           OR `having appeared fails or refuses to comply with an order made in the proceedings`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where the third party (or, where applicable, any other interested party referred to in Rule 3(3)"

-- src:7393 | (3) Where a claimant, having filed an affidavit of claim under Rule 4, does not appear on the hearing of the application under that Rule or, having appeared, fails or refuses to comply with an order made in the proceedings, the Court may make an order declaring the claimant, and all persons claiming under him or her, forever barred from bringing any claim against the third party.
@ref O 63 r 5(3) (src:7393)
GIVEN `the claimant filed an affidavit of claim under Rule 4` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant does not appear on the hearing of the application under that Rule` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant appeared but fails or refuses to comply with an order made in the proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 63 r 5(3) the Court may declare the claimant forever barred` MEANS
    IF `the claimant filed an affidavit of claim under Rule 4` AND (`the claimant does not appear on the hearing of the application under that Rule` OR `the claimant appeared but fails or refuses to comply with an order made in the proceedings`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a claimant, having filed an affidavit of claim under Rule 4, does not appear on the hearing of the application under that Rule or, having appeared, fails or refuses to comply with an order made in the proceedings"

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Rule 6 -- other powers`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:7395 | 6. Subject to Rules 1 to 5, the Court may in or for the purposes of any proceedings in this Order, make such order as to costs or any other matter as the Court thinks just.
@ref O 63 r 6 (src:7395)
GIVEN `the order is in or for the purposes of proceedings in this Order` IS A BOOLEAN
      `one of Rules 1 to 5 provides otherwise on the matter` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 63 r 6 the Court may make such order as to costs or any other matter as it thinks just` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the order is in or for the purposes of proceedings in this Order`)
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the power is given "in or for the purposes of any proceedings in this Order"
        IF `one of Rules 1 to 5 provides otherwise on the matter`
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the power is "Subject to Rules 1 to 5" and where one of them speaks this Rule neither grants nor denies; QA: NOTHING (a displaced grant grants nothing) / other: JUST FALSE
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Rule 7 -- trial of issue stated`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:7397 | 7. —(1) Order 15 applies, with the necessary modifications, to the trial of an issue stated under Rule 5(1)( f ) as it applies to the trial of an action. (2) The Court by whom an issue stated is tried may give such judgment or make such order as finally to dispose of all questions arising in the proceedings to try the issues stated.
@ref O 63 r 7(1) (src:7397)
GIVEN `the trial is of an issue stated under Rule 5(1)(f)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 63 r 7(1) Order 15 applies to the trial of the issue` MEANS
    IF `the trial is of an issue stated under Rule 5(1)(f)`
    THEN JUST TRUE -- Order 15 applies "with the necessary modifications"; what they are is not in this Order (S-L1: applies with changes, and what changes is NOTHING)
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): rule 7(1) speaks of "the trial of an issue stated under Rule 5(1)(f)"

-- src:7397 | 7. —(1) Order 15 applies, with the necessary modifications, to the trial of an issue stated under Rule 5(1)( f ) as it applies to the trial of an action. (2) The Court by whom an issue stated is tried may give such judgment or make such order as finally to dispose of all questions arising in the proceedings to try the issues stated.
@ref O 63 r 7(2) (src:7397)
GIVEN `the Court is the Court by whom an issue stated is tried` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 63 r 7(2) the Court may give such judgment or make such order as finally to dispose of all questions` MEANS
    IF `the Court is the Court by whom an issue stated is tried`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the power is given to "The Court by whom an issue stated is tried"

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Rule 8 -- application by the Authority`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- Order 62 rules 6, 7, 8, 10 and 12 apply "with the necessary modifications" (S-L1: applies; the modifications are NOTHING).
-- src:7399 | 8. —(1) Order 62, Rules 6, 7, 8, 10 and 12 apply, with the necessary modifications, in relation to an application by the Authority under this Order as they apply in relation to a civil penalty action. (2) For the purpose of paragraph (1), a reference in Order 62, Rule 8 to the defendant is a reference to the person referred to in section 236L(1)( a ), ( b ) or ( c ) (as the case may be) or the third party.
@ref O 63 r 8(1) (src:7399)
GIVEN `the application is one by the Authority under this Order` IS A BOOLEAN
      `rule number of Order 62` IS A STRING
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 63 r 8(1) a rule of Order 62 applies to the application` MEANS
    IF `the application is one by the Authority under this Order` AND elem `rule number of Order 62` (LIST
        "6",
        "7",
        "8",
        "10",
        "12")
    THEN JUST TRUE -- applies "with the necessary modifications"; what they are is not in this Order (S-L1)
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): only "Order 62, Rules 6, 7, 8, 10 and 12" are named, and only for an application by the Authority; the paragraph says nothing of other rules or applicants

-- For the purpose of paragraph (1), "the defendant" in Order 62 rule 8 is the person referred to in section 236L(1)(a), (b)
-- or (c) (as the case may be) or the third party.  A STRING result, so no JUST FALSE: the other cases are NOTHING.
-- src:7399 | 8. —(1) Order 62, Rules 6, 7, 8, 10 and 12 apply, with the necessary modifications, in relation to an application by the Authority under this Order as they apply in relation to a civil penalty action. (2) For the purpose of paragraph (1), a reference in Order 62, Rule 8 to the defendant is a reference to the person referred to in section 236L(1)( a ), ( b ) or ( c ) (as the case may be) or the third party.
@ref O 63 r 8(2) (src:7399)
GIVEN `the reference is in Order 62 rule 8 to the defendant` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is read for the purpose of paragraph (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE STRING
`o 63 r 8(2) a reference to the defendant in Order 62 rule 8 is a reference to` MEANS
    IF `the reference is in Order 62 rule 8 to the defendant` AND `it is read for the purpose of paragraph (1)`
    THEN JUST "the person referred to in section 236L(1)(a), (b) or (c) (as the case may be) or the third party"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "For the purpose of paragraph (1), a reference in Order 62, Rule 8 to the defendant" reads only that reference
